The first reconstruction has exposed two concrete audit pressures. First, Riemann–Hurwitz gives 35 raw local partition signatures, while Fig. 8 prints only 20; the paper does not supply the 35→20 filter under its weakened “one exceptional pair” rule. Second, Lemma 3.14 gives no termination invariant for compatible local blocks (for example, why an additional compatible degree-2 block cannot extend a Fig. 11 chain). I’m testing those as named gap candidates rather than treating brevity itself as a defect. I also found a likely swapped \(\\tilde a/\\tilde b\) sentence on p. 16: (4.1) matches the visually left and right blocks in the opposite order from the prose.
