+The canonical formula at (\widetilde g_1) and the same telescoping identity
+through (m) reduce to
+
+\[
+0=1+\det\widetilde L_\infty+(D+d)(d+1)
+ -\sum_{j=1}^{m}\mu_j(d_j-1)D_{j-1}.
+\]
+
+The tail (\mu_j=d+1) is ((d+1)(D-D_p)), leaving precisely (2.12).
